\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {KGA}{} system architecture. Labelled calibration scores and an unlabelled test batch enter the pipeline. The label-free evidence $Z$ is computed first; then a finite-sample certificate $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \Delta $}\mathaccent "0362{\Delta }\pm \varepsilon $ is formed at level $\alpha $; finally the trichotomy maps the certificate to one of three actions. The adaptation mechanism (Tent, EATA, SAR, or any other) is a plug-in; \textsc  {KGA}{} wraps it without modification. }}{69}{figure.6.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kga-arch}{{6.1}{69}{\KGA {} system architecture. Labelled calibration scores and an unlabelled test batch enter the pipeline. The label-free evidence $Z$ is computed first; then a finite-sample certificate $\widehat \Delta \pm \varepsilon $ is formed at level $\alpha $; finally the trichotomy maps the certificate to one of three actions. The adaptation mechanism (Tent, EATA, SAR, or any other) is a plug-in; \KGA {} wraps it without modification}{figure.6.1}{}}
