\newlabel{thm:bit-necessity}{{C.10}{180}{Necessity: every identifying assumption is a bit-selector}{theorem.C.10}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.9}{\ignorespaces The one-bit theorem, validated. Left (Thm~\ref {thm:flip-witness}): the flip witness $P'$ matches the full evidence law of $P$ (TV $=0$; identical agreement products) while every advantage and benefit sign is negated. Right (Thm~\ref {thm:onebit-id}): label-free recovery of $b$ up to the bit at the $m^{-1/2}$ rate (log-log slope $-0.51$).}}{181}{figure.C.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:onebit}{{C.9}{181}{The one-bit theorem, validated. Left (Thm~\ref {thm:flip-witness}): the flip witness $P'$ matches the full evidence law of $P$ (TV $=0$; identical agreement products) while every advantage and benefit sign is negated. Right (Thm~\ref {thm:onebit-id}): label-free recovery of $b$ up to the bit at the $m^{-1/2}$ rate (log-log slope $-0.51$)}{figure.C.9}{}}
\newlabel{thm:bit-dictionary}{{C.11}{181}{The dictionary: published devices select the same bit}{theorem.C.11}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.10}{\ignorespaces The budget audit (Thms~\ref {thm:audit},~\ref {thm:no-verify}). Sound at level $\alpha $ under a true budget; power $1.000$ against violations beyond the radius (bootstrap); correctly blind on the bit-ambiguous set $\mathcal  B_\beta $ and on the rank-one-preserving stealth law ($\tau \approx 0$) --- the two provably irreducible blind zones; $\tau $ rises with overt error-correlation $\rho $ (Pearson $0.914$).}}{182}{figure.C.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:audit}{{C.10}{182}{The budget audit (Thms~\ref {thm:audit},~\ref {thm:no-verify}). Sound at level $\alpha $ under a true budget; power $1.000$ against violations beyond the radius (bootstrap); correctly blind on the bit-ambiguous set $\mathcal B_\beta $ and on the rank-one-preserving stealth law ($\tau \approx 0$) --- the two provably irreducible blind zones; $\tau $ rises with overt error-correlation $\rho $ (Pearson $0.914$)}{figure.C.10}{}}
